    "sha": "53881c9274b49b770d0625131d6ff1f00dc3e511",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKDUzODgxYzkyNzRiNDliNzcwZDA2MjUxMzFkNmZmMWYwMGRjM2U1MTE",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-19T17:04:29Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-19T17:04:29Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(2d): drop near-zero loops from the pocket region on a part\n\nThe pocket region on a part is the enclosed area minus the part material\nthat stands in it. The two tessellations of a shared wall left 3-point\nloops of about 1e-8 mm2 in that difference. A clockwise one stands\noutside each boundary, so Region::triangles refused the region and the\narea preview of the biggest fig8 patch had no fill with the default\nContainment.\n\nminus_standing now removes each loop below ISLAND_AREA_MIN with the new\nRegion::without_slivers, which filters loops and changes no kept loop.\nThe same region goes to generation.\n\nPins: area_preview_of_the_default_containment_is_filled (ui lib),\nregion_slivers (geometry).\n\nFixes #2766\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
